---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About Santi Solis | LGBTQ+ Tulum Guide | Queerness Experiences" description={"Meet Santi Solis (they/them), a queer, trans, nonbinary, Mexican former UCLA wildlife biologist who's called Tulum home since 2017 and founded Queerness Experiences, an LGBTQ+ travel company in Tulum."}>

<section class="guide about-hero" id="about" style="border-top:none;position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
  <div class="shape-y"></div>
  <div class="shape-t"></div>
  <div class="guide-inner" style="position:relative;z-index:2;">
    <p class="sec-eye" style="color:var(--yellow);position:relative;z-index:2;">About</p>
    <h1>I'm Santi.<br>Nice to meet you.</h1>
    <p class="guide-lead">Queer, nonbinary, Mexican, and a Tulum local since 2017. I create travel experiences for queer, trans, and nonbinary people, rooted in the places and people that actually make this town special. My pronouns are they/them.</p>
    <div class="hero-grid" style="width:100%;max-width:520px;">
      <img src="/images/santi-hero-tulum.jpg" alt="Santi laughing in the water near Tulum, wearing a life vest">
      <img src="/images/santi-iglta-guadalajara.jpg" alt="Santi speaking on a panel at the IGLTA LGBTQ+ Travel Symposium in Guadalajara">
      <img src="/images/santi-pattie-gonia-scholarship.jpg" alt="Santi hugging a drag queen in the mountains, from the Pattie Gonia Queer Outdoor Expedition scholarship">
      <img src="/images/santi-market-ucla.jpg" alt="Santi laughing with a friend at a local market in Tulum">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-hero .shape-y{height:15%;}
  .about-hero h1{-webkit-text-stroke:1.5px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);paint-order:stroke fill;max-width:640px;position:relative;z-index:2;}
  .about-hero .guide-lead,.about-hero .guide-photo{position:relative;z-index:2;}
  .about-hero .guide-lead{font-size:20px;}
  .story-photo-landscape{width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;object-fit:cover;border:3px solid var(--dark);box-shadow:6px 6px 0 var(--yellow);margin-bottom:var(--s-md);}
  .about-creds.creds{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;max-width:none;margin:0;}
  .about-creds .cred .ct{font-size:15px;}
  .about-creds .cred .cd{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;}
  .about-creds .cred{padding:14px;}
</style>

<section class="creds about-creds" aria-label="Credentials" style="background:var(--bone);padding:var(--s-md) var(--s-sm) var(--s-lg);">
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">01</div><div><div class="ct">Former UCLA Wildlife Biologist</div><div class="cd">I studied marmots. The science behind every nature-based tour.</div></div></div>
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">02</div><div><div class="ct">Conference Speaker</div><div class="cd">Invited by the Guadalajara tourism board to speak on a panel about creating queer experiences at IGLTA's conference.</div></div></div>
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">03</div><div><div class="ct">Women's Day Speaker &amp; MC</div><div class="cd">Led a talk to 300+ women across Latin America on expanding their comfort zones, and served as master of ceremonies for Women's Day in Tulum.</div></div></div>
  <div class="cred"><div class="cnum">04</div><div><div class="ct">Committee Member, LADLE</div><div class="cd">Los Amigos de la Esquina. Started as an original volunteer, later general manager, now on committee.</div></div></div>
</section>

<section style="background:var(--white);padding:var(--s-sm) var(--s-sm) 0;text-align:center;">
  <p style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted);">I also work with other queer and trans travel agencies, helping them create experiences that prioritize small businesses and connection with locals. <a href="/work-with-me" style="color:var(--magenta);font-weight:700;">See how we could work together →</a></p>
</section>

<section style="background:var(--white);padding:var(--s-md) var(--s-sm) var(--s-lg);max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;">
  <p class="sec-eye">My story</p>
  <img class="story-photo-landscape" src="/images/santi-dog-lagoon.jpg" alt="Santi sitting with a dog on a dock over the lagoon in Tulum" style="aspect-ratio:4/3;object-position:center 45%;">
  <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--dark);margin-bottom:var(--s-sm);">I was born in Chiapas, the Mexican state that borders Guatemala, though my family is from Mexico City. We moved to New York when I was three, then to LA when I was four. I moved to Tulum in 2017 expecting to stay for three months, and here I am all these years later. Before moving to Tulum, I was a wildlife biologist for a UCLA research lab based out of the Rocky Mountains. Now I run travel experiences for queer, trans, and nonbinary people who want the real Tulum, not a resort version of it.</p>
  <img class="story-photo-landscape" src="/images/santi-birding-binoculars.jpg" alt="Santi holding binoculars while birding in the jungle near Tulum" style="aspect-ratio:4/3;object-position:center 20%;">
  <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--dark);margin-bottom:var(--s-sm);">Outside of tours, I'm part of a local theater group and take go-go dancing classes. I also serve on the committee for Los Amigos de la Esquina (LADLE), a local nonprofit offering art, wellbeing, and life-skills programs for Mayan and local Mexican kids. I started there as a volunteer, later became general manager, and now help guide the organization from the committee.</p>
  <img class="story-photo-landscape" src="/images/la-guarida-workshop-group.jpg" alt="A community workshop at La Guarida, part of the LADLE nonprofit in Tulum" style="margin-bottom:0;">
</section>

<section style="background:var(--magenta);padding:var(--s-lg) var(--s-sm);text-align:center;">
  <p style="max-width:520px;margin:0 auto var(--s-md);font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--white);">Want to come explore Tulum with me?</p>
  <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:14px;">
    <a href="/tours" class="btn-p" style="display:inline-block;">See the Tours →</a>
    <a href="/blog/queer-tulum-recommendations" class="btn-p" style="display:inline-block;">Free Recommendations →</a>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
